In particular, I'd like to see a "Runstop" option (as in omega) where you
run until you find something "interesting," as for example the door to a
room.  Since we all know NH is _much_ better coded than any of the others,
the dev team could probably even set it up so you can define what you find
"interesting."

(Similarly, I'd like to see the "pickup" option be more flexible.  It's
currently ON/OFF.  I recently suggested "goldonly" as a third option, and
someone else -- I forget who -- suggested a pickup option with a string, which
you could set, as for example "$!?[" to pick up money, potions, scrolls, armor,
and nothing else automatically.)


>	2.  In NetHack, if you want to know about something in a space in 
>the room that you are not stepping on, you have to use the "/" directive 
>and then place the cursor.  That's nice, but Moria has a similar, 
>directional "examine" command (I think it is "x" or "X" or something) 
>which is a lot more convenient.  

Actually, the NH / command has the advantage that you can use it to identify
_anything_ on the level that you already know about.  For example, if you did
a scroll of magic mapping and it shows an altar, you can use "/" to find out
its alignment without trekking all the way across the level to find out.


