>	1.  I know this is a FAQ, but what is the fastest way to change 
>the  alignment of an altar?

Depends on what you want to change it _to_.  If you're chaotic and want to 
change the altar to chaotic, sacrificing a human corpse _always_ works (if
it's fresh enough to eat.  Don't bother sacrificing zombies, mummies, etc.,
and don't haul them more than one room or so to sacrifice.)  It also sometimes
summons a demon, who's usually "peaceful."

Other than that, just keep #O ffering fresh corpses.  Eventually it will
be converted.

Note:  Failed conversions can negatively affect your luck.  Be careful!


>	2.  If I'm changing my alignment by sacrifice to another altar, 
>how can I tell if I'm changing my own alignment or converting the altar? 
>What does "You feel the powers of X lessen" really mean?

It means that you failed to convert the altar.  You'll know if you manage
to convert yourself.  (It generally only happens when your god is pissed
at you.)


>	3.  What the hell is an athame?  How do you correctly say that 
>word? Why doesn't it dull?

It's a of thin sword used in blood magick.  The first "a" is pronounced
as in "mat," the second is long as in "dame," and the "e" is silent.
It doesn't dull because that's the way the code was written.


